  "abstract_summary": "A language model deployed as an agent arrives at every session with the weights it was trained with, so anything it learns in deployment has to be held somewhere else. External memory is now a standard answer to that problem. A store that an agent writes, reads and summarises for itself, however, can accumulate its...",
